	(text "FleetBus Lite bench: two LP-MSPM0G3507 on a diode wired-AND CAN bus (no transceivers), 500 kbit/s.\nD1/D2: band (cathode) toward each board's PA12 CAN_TX. R1 pulls the bus to 3V3 = recessive; any TX low = dominant.\n+3V3 comes ONLY from U2 (body node) J1_1. U1's 3V3 stays unconnected: never join the two boards' 3V3.\nSilence U1 for heartbeat-loss tests by holding its NRST, not by unplugging it (an unpowered TX pin jams the bus through D1).\nJ1 = Analog Discovery logic input (DIO0, CAN decoder) + GND. All grounds common.\nPin numbers are header_pin of each 10-pin header in the ECE319K symbol (J4_9 = PA12, J4_10 = PA13). Firmware map: firmware/bsp/mspm0g3507/bsp_pins.h."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
